UID:international-lam-research-conference-lamposium-2025@mtor-atlas.org
DTSTAMP:20261018T180043Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250929
SUMMARY:International LAM Research Conference & LAMposium 2025
LOCATION:Westin Kansas City at Crown Center\, Kansas City\, MO\, USA
DESCRIPTION:The LAM Foundation's marquee event: a dual-track meeting combin
 ing a scientific research conference (>100 researchers and clinicians) wit
 h a patient and family conference\; >300 attendees. Held every two to thre
 e years in rotating locations. NEXT EDITION NOT YET ANNOUNCED as of July 2
 026 - this record documents the 2025 edition\; add the next edition when d
 ated.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★★★): LAM is the second approved m
 TOR-inhibitor indication (sirolimus\, via the MILES trial) and the only di
 sease in the world whose standard of care IS mTOR inhibition. The single m
 ost concentrated venue for human sirolimus efficacy and long-term safety d
 ata. Atlas authors: McCormack FX\, Moss J.\n\nConference site: https://www
 .thelamfoundation.org/lamposium/lamposium-research-conference/\n\nIn Olive
 r's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-international-lam-resear
 ch-conference-lamposium-2025
URL:https://www.thelamfoundation.org/lamposium/lamposium-research-conferenc
 e/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4th-prague-symposium-on-cancer-metabolism-2025@mtor-atlas.org
DTSTAMP:20261018T180043Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251014
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20251016
SUMMARY:4th Prague Symposium on Cancer Metabolism 2025
LOCATION:Plzeňská Campus\, Pelouch Lecture Hall\, Prague\, Czech Republic
DESCRIPTION:Fourth edition of a deliberately small cancer-metabolism meetin
 g run by the CLIP metabolic study group at the Second Faculty of Medicine\
 , Charles University\, co-organised by the Institute of Biotechnology of t
 he Czech Academy of Sciences. The limited-attendance format is the point: 
 it is built for exchange between students\, researchers and clinicians rat
 her than for a large audience. A Seahorse user meeting at BIOCEV followed 
 on 16 October.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★★★): mTOR is not in the 
 programme title\, which is cancer metabolism\, but David Sabatini is a lis
 ted invited speaker and he is one of the five researchers the Atlas tracks
  most closely (48 studies in the corpus). His speaker biography on the sym
 posium page is almost entirely mTOR: the discovery of the kinase\, mTORC1 
 and mTORC2\, and nutrient signalling to mTORC1 through the lysosomal Rag G
 TPases. Notable for the Atlas as the Prague meeting Sabatini spoke at from
  his IOCB Prague base\, alongside the separate Prague Metabolism and Signa
 ling Symposium already curated here.\n\nSpeakers or organisers with a prof
 ile in the Atlas: David M. Sabatini\, Arkaitz Carracedo\n\nConference site
 : https://www.lf2.cuni.cz/en/events/4th-prague-symposium-on-cancer-metabol
 ism\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-4th-pragu
 e-symposium-on-cancer-metabolism-2025
URL:https://www.lf2.cuni.cz/en/events/4th-prague-symposium-on-cancer-metabo
 lism
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
