SUMMARY:Keystone: Autophagy – Mechanisms to Therapy 2026
LOCATION:Keystone Resort\, Keystone\, Colorado\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Keystone Symposium covering the roles and mechanisms of autopha
 gy across health and disease\, spanning basic\, translational and clinical
  research plus industry developments. Held jointly with the Keystone sympo
 sium 'Membrane Dynamics\, Repair and Disease' to enable cross-talk.\n\nWhy
  it matters for mTOR (★★): mTORC1 is the master negative regulator of 
 autophagy\; sessions address mTOR inhibition and nutrient control of autop
 hagic flux. Directly relevant to the autophagy/lysosome arm of the Atlas.\
 n\nSpeakers or organisers with a profile in the Atlas: James H. Hurley\, J
 ayanta Debnath\, J. Wade Harper\, Sharon A. Tooze\n\nConference site: http
 s://www.keystonesymposia.org/conferences/conference-listing/meeting/p12026
 \n\nIn Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-keystone-aut
 ophagy-mechanisms-to-therapy-2026
