DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260209
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260213
SUMMARY:Keystone: Mitochondria Signaling in Physiology and Disease 2026
LOCATION:Keystone Resort\, Keystone\, Colorado\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Keystone Symposium on mitochondria as signaling organelles that
  control cellular and organismal physiology\, and how mitochondrial dysfun
 ction drives disease.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★): Mitochondrial meta
 bolism and nutrient status are tightly integrated with mTORC1 signaling\; 
 mitochondrial cues feed into growth control central to the Atlas. Downgrad
 ed to Tier 3: mTOR is not a named topic anywhere in the program – the co
 nnection is inferred adjacency (mitochondrial cues feeding nutrient sensin
 g)\, not stated content. Retained for completeness\, not prioritised.\n\nS
 peakers or organisers with a profile in the Atlas: Liron Bar-Peled\, Reube
 n J. Shaw\n\nConference site: https://www.keystonesymposia.org/conferences
 /conference-listing/meeting/b12026\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor
 -atlas.org/events/#ev-keystone-mitochondria-signaling-in-physiology-and-di
 sease-20-908fa
