 r-atlas.org
DTSTAMP:20261018T180043Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260322
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260326
SUMMARY:Keystone Symposia: Aging – Immune Function and Organ Health 2026
LOCATION:Fairmont Banff Springs\, Banff\, AB\, Canada
DESCRIPTION:Keystone Symposia conference on the role of the immune system i
 n aging and its impact on organ health\, longevity and rejuvenation. Held 
 jointly with the Keystone Symposium on Innate Immunity: Diversity in Host 
 Defense and Disease. Sessions covered targeting innate immunity for health
 y aging\, inflammation/senescence\, organ regeneration and aging\, inflamm
 aging\, organ-organ communication and systemic aging\, and biomarkers/agin
 g clocks/human longevity.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★★): Not an mTOR
 -focused meeting\, but a top-tier geroscience venue whose organisers and s
 peakers set the framing for nutrient-sensing and gerotherapeutic work the 
 Atlas tracks (senescence\, inflammaging\, rejuvenation\, aging clocks). Re
 levance to mTOR is indirect: no session on the programme addresses mTORC1/
 mTORC2 or rapamycin directly.\n\nSpeakers or organisers with a profile in 
 the Atlas: Anne Brunet\n\nConference site: https://www.keystonesymposia.or
 g/conferences/conference-listing/meeting/l82026\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR Atlas:
  https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-keystone-symposia-aging-immune-function
 -and-organ-health-202-n9orlx
