DESCRIPTION:One-day in-person meeting of the New York Academy of Sciences C
 ancer and Signaling Discussion Group\, co-presented with NYU Langone Healt
 h\, on how tumour cells exploit signalling and metabolic pathways in the t
 umour microenvironment to drive malignant growth. Concluded\; the 2027 edi
 tion of the same recurring meeting is also in the Atlas.\n\nWhy it matters
  for mTOR (★): Same basis as the 2027 successor already in the Atlas: a 
 cancer-metabolism meeting rather than an mTOR meeting. PI3K-AKT-mTOR signa
 lling is standard content in this field but was not named in the announced
  scope. Listed for the record because this is the edition Brendan Manning 
 and Christian Dibble referenced on Bluesky — neither is named on any off
 icial NYAS page\, so their involvement is unconfirmed (same caveat as the 
 2027 record).\n\nConference site: https://www.nyas.org/shaping-science/eve
 nts/cancer-metabolism-and-signaling-in-the-tumor-microenvironment-2026/\n\
