BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mtor-node-symposium-2026-3rd-annual@mtor-atlas.org
DTSTAMP:20261018T180043Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260605
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260606
SUMMARY:mTOR Node Symposium 2026 (3rd Annual)
LOCATION:King's College London\, London\, UK
DESCRIPTION:Third annual research meeting of the UK mTOR Pathway Diseases n
 ode (NIHR/MRC-funded initiative)\, convening ~70 researchers\, clinicians\
 , industry representatives and patients around the 14 known rare diseases 
 caused by mutations in mTOR-pathway genes (~10\,000 people affected in the
  UK).\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★★★): The only meeting in the cale
 ndar organized around mTOR-pathway diseases as its sole subject\, not just
  an adjacent topic. Discovery-science session explicitly covered phosphopr
 oteomics\, EV biomarkers\, patient-derived assembloids\, cellular ageing m
 odels\, and 'the broader relevance of mTOR signalling across rare and age-
 related diseases' – directly on-topic for the Atlas's clinic/translation
  branch. No named external invited-speaker roster was published in the pub
 lic writeup (a PPIE patient/clinical meeting\, not a standard academic pro
 gram)\, so Linked_Authors is left empty\; node leadership is captured in O
 rganizers instead.\n\nConference site: https://www.kcl.ac.uk/news/symposiu
 m-brings-together-rare-disease-community-to-accelerate-mtor-research\n\nIn
  Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-mtor-node-symposiu
 m-2026-3rd-annual
URL:https://www.kcl.ac.uk/news/symposium-brings-together-rare-disease-commu
 nity-to-accelerate-mtor-research
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
