 e program's explicit 'Beyond AMPK: nutrient-sensing pathways' and 'AMPK fa
 mily in cancer\, aging and longevity' sessions cover mTOR as the reciproca
 l arm of energy sensing. UPDATE (2026-07-22): official speaker list is now
  published and does NOT include Hardie or Shaw as previously speculated\; 
 confirmed speakers instead include Atlas authors Hongbo Chi (immunometabol
 ism/AMPK-mTOR crosstalk in T cells) and Thomas Weichhart (mTOR/immunometab
 olism)\, both re-linked below in place of Shaw RJ.\n\nSpeakers or organise
 rs with a profile in the Atlas: Hongbo Chi\, Thomas Weichhart\n\nConferenc
 e site: https://www.atoutcom.com/ampk/\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://
