SUMMARY:Keystone Symposia: Tumor and Host Metabolism – Integrating Molecu
 lar\, Cellular\, and Systemic Interactions 2027
LOCATION:Ludwig Institute Princeton University\, Princeton\, NJ\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Keystone Symposium\, presented in partnership with the Ludwig I
 nstitute for Cancer Research (Princeton Branch)\, on interactions between 
 tumor and host metabolism: how environmental and whole-body changes\, diet
 \, and aging affect tumor growth and progression.\n\nWhy it matters for mT
 OR (★★): Successor to the Atlas's existing 'Tumor Metabolism' Keystone
  entry (2026). Direct mTORC1 relevance via Andrea Ballabio's confirmed tal
 k 'Paracrine Activation of mTORC1 in the Tumor Microenvironment'\; a dedic
 ated Day-3 session ('Frontiers in Stress Responses and Aging in Cancer') c
 overs aging-cancer metabolic crosstalk. Co-organized by Marcia Haigis (Co-
 Director\, Paul F. Glenn Center for the Biology of Aging at Harvard) and L
 ydia Lynch (Princeton/Ludwig).\n\nSpeakers or organisers with a profile in
  the Atlas: Hongbo Chi\, Andrea Ballabio\, Jonathan D. Powell\n\nConferenc
 e site: https://www.keystonesymposia.org/conferences/conference-listing/me
 eting/P12027\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-
 keystone-symposia-tumor-and-host-metabolism-integrating-mole-rqwfsh
URL:https://www.keystonesymposia.org/conferences/conference-listing/meeting
 /P12027
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
