SUMMARY:Keystone Symposia: Integrative Mitochondrial Medicine 2027
LOCATION:Fairmont Banff Springs\, Banff\, Canada
DESCRIPTION:Keystone Symposia conference on integrative mitochondrial medic
 ine\, spanning mitochondrial genome editing\, synthetic biology\, imaging\
 , precision medicine for mitochondrial disease\, and mitochondrial transpl
 antation.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★): Mitochondrial quality control\
 , biogenesis and dynamics are tightly coupled to mTOR/AMPK nutrient-sensin
 g signaling (mitophagy\, PGC-1alpha-driven biogenesis)\; direct companion 
 event to the Atlas's existing 'Mitochondria Signaling in Physiology and Di
 sease' Keystone meeting. Same basis as that entry: mTOR is not a named pro
 gram topic\, the connection is inferred mechanistic adjacency. Retained fo
 r completeness\, not prioritised.\n\nSpeakers or organisers with a profile
  in the Atlas: Vamsi K. Mootha\n\nConference site: https://www.keystonesym
 posia.org/conferences/conference-listing/meeting/C42027\n\nIn Oliver's mTO
 R Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-keystone-symposia-integrative-m
 itochondrial-medicine-2027
URL:https://www.keystonesymposia.org/conferences/conference-listing/meeting
 /C42027
