UID:fusion-translational-control-from-cells-to-organisms-2027@mtor-atlas.or
 g
DTSTAMP:20261018T180043Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270522
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270526
SUMMARY:Fusion: Translational Control – From Cells to Organisms 2027
LOCATION:Meliá Durrës\, Durrës\, Albania
DESCRIPTION:Fusion Conferences residential meeting on the regulation of pro
 tein synthesis from single molecules to whole organisms\, with emphasis on
  ribosome heterogeneity and translational rewiring in cancer. Appears to b
 e the inaugural edition\; no edition number is printed.\n\nWhy it matters 
 for mTOR (★★): The best-characterised output of mTORC1 is cap-dependen
 t translation\, through phosphorylation of 4E-BP1 and S6K1\, and this meet
 ing is where that branch of the pathway is treated as its own field rather
  than as a downstream readout. Chaired in part by Davide Ruggero\, who has
  three studies in the Atlas\, and sitting in the Sonenberg lineage of tran
 slational control. Relevant to the question of which mTORC1 substrates are
  rapamycin-resistant\, which is exactly where rapamycin and bi-steric inhi
 bitors diverge.\n\nSpeakers or organisers with a profile in the Atlas: Dav
 ide Ruggero\n\nConference site: https://fusion-conferences.com/conference/
 213\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-fusion-tr
 anslational-control-from-cells-to-organisms-2027
URL:https://fusion-conferences.com/conference/213
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fusion-2nd-redox-biology-in-health-disease-2027@mtor-atlas.org
DTSTAMP:20261018T180043Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270525
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270529
SUMMARY:Fusion: 2nd Redox Biology in Health & Disease 2027
LOCATION:Meliá Durrës\, Durrës\, Albania
DESCRIPTION:Second edition of the Fusion Conferences meeting on redox contr
 ol (ROS\, NAD\, glutathione) in cellular health\, cancer\, ageing\, neurod
 egeneration and cardiometabolic disease. The first edition ran 3-6 Nov 202
 5 in Tulum\, Mexico.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★): Relevance comes fro
 m the attendee list\, not from the programme\, which is exactly what tier 
 3 is for. The announced theme is redox control (ROS\, NAD\, glutathione\, 
 ferroptosis) and mTOR is nowhere in it. What makes this meeting matter to 
 the Atlas is that the published invited-speaker list contains both Brendan
  D. Manning and David M. Sabatini\, the two most heavily represented autho
 rs in the corpus (10 and 46 studies)\, alongside Eileen White and Matthew 
 Vander Heiden. That is the strongest author overlap of any meeting in this
  table. The mechanistic link that does exist runs through oxidative regula
 tion of the TSC complex and the shared metabolite pool supporting anabolis
 m\, but it is inference\, not billed content.\n\nSpeakers or organisers wi
 th a profile in the Atlas: Brendan D. Manning\, David M. Sabatini\n\nConfe
 rence site: https://fusion-conferences.com/conference/211\n\nIn Oliver's m
 TOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-fusion-2nd-redox-biology-in-h
 ealth-disease-2027
URL:https://fusion-conferences.com/conference/211
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
