SUMMARY:Gordon Research Conference: Biology of Aging 2027
LOCATION:Renaissance Tuscany Il Ciocco\, Lucca (Barga)\, Italy
DESCRIPTION:Long-running (since 1962) flagship Gordon Research Conference o
 n the biology of aging\, held biennially\, alternating US/Europe venues. B
 rings together the core international aging-biology research community acr
 oss molecular\, cellular\, and organismal scales.\n\nWhy it matters for mT
 OR (★★): mTOR/nutrient-sensing signaling (rapamycin\, TOR pathway\, au
 tophagy) has been a recurring major session theme at prior editions of thi
 s conference given its central role in aging biology\; a flagship venue fo
 r mTOR-and-aging primary research even when not named in the title.\n\nCon
 ference site: https://www.grc.org/biology-of-aging-conference/2027/\n\nIn 
 Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-gordon-research-con
 ference-biology-of-aging-2027
