 org
DTSTAMP:20261018T180043Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270809
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270812
SUMMARY:FASEB SRC: Nutrient Sensing and Signaling in Metabolism 2027
LOCATION:The Galt House Hotel\, Louisville\, KY\, USA
DESCRIPTION:2027 FASEB Science Research Conference on nutrient sensing and 
 metabolic signalling: how cells and whole organisms adapt to changing nutr
 ient states\, and how defects in those mechanisms underlie metabolic disea
 se. The meeting is pitched at the level of insulin-responsive metabolic ti
 ssues and integrated physiology\, with obesity\, diabetes\, MASLD\, cardio
 vascular disease\, skeletal muscle atrophy\, cancer and aging named as the
  clinical areas covered. Co-located with The Molecular Metabolism Conferen
 ce: From Cell Biology to Systems Physiology\, and includes Meet the Expert
 s dine-around sessions and career-development sessions for early-career sc
 ientists.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★★★): Nutrient sensing and met
 abolic signalling are the named subject of the whole conference\, not a ne
 ighbouring theme. Brendan D. Manning (Harvard)\, one of the five researche
 rs the Atlas tracks most closely and the author of 11 studies in the corpu
 s\, is one of the two conference organizers\; the organizing role is liste
 d on the FASEB conference page. No invited-speaker list had been published
  as of 9 Oct 2026\, so the mTOR content of individual sessions cannot yet 
 be read off the programme.\n\nSpeakers or organisers with a profile in the
  Atlas: Brendan D. Manning\n\nConference site: https://www.faseb.org/meeti
 ngs-and-events/science-research-conferences/nutrient-sensing-and-signaling
 -in-metabolism-2027\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/even
 ts/#ev-faseb-src-nutrient-sensing-and-signaling-in-metabolism-2027
URL:https://www.faseb.org/meetings-and-events/science-research-conferences/
 nutrient-sensing-and-signaling-in-metabolism-2027
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
